// The bitmap font the text drawer paints with — bits, not texels.
//
// It lives in pdklib/ and not in pdk/ because the console has no idea what a letter
// is: on a PSX the font was an ASSET the game shipped, uploaded into video RAM
// like any other texture, and drawn with the same textured primitives as the
// scenery. Nothing here is a hardware feature; it is a disc's own picture of the
// alphabet, kept in one place so every disc does not redraw it.
//
// The design is the era's: a 5x7 ink area inside an 8x8 CELL. Three blank columns
// on the right and one blank row at the bottom ARE the letter spacing — that is
// what makes a monospaced advance of exactly one cell work with no kerning table
// and no per-glyph width. Eight is not decoration either: an 8-wide cell makes
// every cell start on an even texel, which is what keeps the IDX4 packing in
// rv_text.hpp free of half-byte shifts (see the THEOREM there).
//
// Storage: 8 bytes per glyph, one byte per row, top row first. Within a row the
// HIGH bit (0x80) is the LEFTMOST pixel — the order the rows are written in when
// a human draws them as hex, and the reason the low three bits of every entry are
// zero. A set bit means ink.
//
// Glyphs are indexed by ASCII code minus 32, so index 0 is the space and index 94
// is '~'. Index 95 is the NOTDEF cell: a solid 8x8 block, deliberately the ugliest
// thing in the table, because a byte outside 32..126 must be VISIBLE. Text that
// silently loses characters looks like a text bug; a row of black slabs looks like
// what it is, an encoding problem.

inline constexpr int rv_font_cell_width = 8;   // advance and atlas cell, in texels
inline constexpr int rv_font_cell_height = 8;  // rows per glyph, and bytes per glyph
inline constexpr int rv_font_ink_width = 5;    // columns a glyph actually draws in
inline constexpr int rv_font_ink_height = 7;   // rows a glyph actually draws in

inline constexpr int rv_font_first_code = 32;   // ' '
inline constexpr int rv_font_last_code = 126;   // '~'
inline constexpr int rv_font_glyph_count = 96;  // 95 printable + notdef
inline constexpr int rv_font_notdef_index = 95;

